codex
The patch adds the intended backfill path, but it can wedge projection processing for arbitrary public node kinds and can still produce false-ready state after no-embedder deferral followed by a write. These are correctness issues in normal governed flows.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Don't enrol kinds the vector writer can't commit — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s20c/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:16950-16951
  When a corpus contains a public `PreparedWrite::Node` kind outside `resolve_source_type`'s locked list (for example `"invoice"`), declaring a vector projection now registers that kind and makes the scheduler pick it up. `commit_projection_outcomes` then fails before recording a terminal because `resolve_source_type(kind)` returns `Storage`, so the row remains pending forever and `drain()` times out. Either restrict enrolment to commit-able kinds or make the vector writer handle arbitrary node kinds.

- [P2] Backfill stranded rows when late-enrolling a kind — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s20c/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:4847-4847
  If a database persisted a `searchable→vector` projection while opened without an embedder, then later reopens with an embedder and writes the same kind before re-applying the projection, this path registers the kind but only the new row is enqueued. Older rows written under the no-embedder session keep their `up_to_date` terminals with no vector row, so after the new row drains, readiness can report ready while pre-existing vector-eligible rows remain unembedded.
